[006]  P│ Initiatives  >  Improve shared-con…  >  pi-shared-context-…  >  Description                 │
[007]   │> Select shared-context projects through interactive breadcrumbs · Description               │
[008] [E│                                                                                             │
[009]   │  ## What to build                                                                           │
[010] /r│                                                                                             │edb
[011] ac│  Add the Projects view to the shared-context modal. Users open this view through a          │
[012]   │  focusable, clickable Projects breadcrumb. Users select a project and browse its existing   │
[013] tu│  tracker and Files workspace.                                                               │
[014] /r│                                                                                             │edb
[015] ac│  Reuse shared-context enumeration and route resolution. Include the current project.        │
[016] /r│  Deduplicate entries by canonical identity. Do not scan unrelated repositories or add       │edb
[017] ac│  another project registry.                                                                  │
[018]   │                                                                                             │
[019]   │  Establish the breadcrumb and focus contract for later tracker screens. The current command │
[020]   │  still opens the current project. Selecting another project changes only the modal context. │
[021]   │                                                                                             │
[022]   │  ## Acceptance criteria                                                                     │
[023]   │                                                                                             │
[024]   │  1. The project list displays a name and origin or stable identity for each project. Equal  │
[025]   │  repository names remain distinguishable.                                                   │
[026]   │  2. Keyboard focus reaches the Projects breadcrumb. Enter activates it. A mouse click       │
[027]   │  activates the same control.                                                                │
[028]   │  3. Selecting a project resolves its routes before record access. The selected project owns │
[029]   │  tracker reads, Files reads, and action targets.                                            │
[030]   │  4. The header displays Shared or Repo from the selected alignment route. The indicator is  │
[031]   │  read-only.                                                                                 │
[032]   │  5. Project selection does not change the active Pi session directory or system             │
[033]   │  instructions.                                                                              │
[034]   │  6. Returning to a project restores its navigation, selection, and scroll position. Each    │
[035]   │  workspace retains independent state.                                                       │
[036]   │  7. Project changes dispose of old watchers and attach the correct new watchers. Old        │
[037]   │  project updates do not change the selected project view.                                   │
[038]   │  8. A project without a usable checkout retains readable context. Checkout-dependent        │
[039]   │  actions display a clear disabled reason.                                                   │
[040]   │                                                                                             │
[041] ──│ [Return]  [PgUp] [PgDn]                                                                     │───
[042]   │↑↓ scroll · PgUp/Dn page · Esc return                                                        │
